      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-168868",
      ":question/problem": "Classify the critical points using the second partial derivatives test.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$ are local maximum since $\\,H(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$0\\,\\,$ and $\\,\\,\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202{x}^{2}}(0,\\pm \\sqrt{5})$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$0$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(0,0)$ is a saddle point since $\\,\\,H(0,0)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$0$"
